Now let me plan the csv-core fixes:

### Fix 1: DFA can't leave `InComment` when `\n` isn't a distinguished byte

In `build_dfa`, after adding all other classes, if comments are enabled and `\n` doesn't yet have its own class, add it:

```rust
// A comment is only ever ended by `\n` (see `transition_nfa`), so when
// comments are enabled, `\n` must be a discriminating byte in the DFA.
// If nothing else already gave it an equivalence class (e.g. a CRLF
// terminator or its use as another special byte), add it now. Without
// this, the DFA would lump `\n` in with the default class and never
// leave the comment state.
if self.comment.is_some() && self.dfa.classes.classes[b'\n' as usize] == 0 {
    self.dfa.classes.add(b'\n');
}
```

Wait — accessing `self.dfa.classes.classes` directly — it's a private field within the same module, fine.

But check TRANS_CLASSES capacity: currently 7. Worst case count of `add` calls: delimiter(1) + quote(1) + escape(1) + comment(1) + CRLF(2) = 6 adds → num_classes = 7. With Any term: 5 adds → 6 classes, +1 for `\n` = 7. ✓ No bump needed.

