```rust
if state == self.dfa.in_field || state == self.dfa.in_quoted {
    self.dfa.classes.scan_and_copy(input, &mut nin, output, &mut nout);
}
```

→

```rust
if state == self.dfa.in_field || state == self.dfa.in_quoted {
    let scanned = nin;
    self.dfa.classes.scan_and_copy(input, &mut nin, output, &mut nout);
    // `scan_and_copy` consumes bytes in the default equivalence class
    // without going through the main loop, so any `\n` bytes it copied
    // would otherwise evade the line counter.
    self.line += count_lfs(&input[scanned..nin]);
}
```

where count_lfs is a small helper:

```rust
#[inline(always)]
fn count_lfs(bytes: &[u8]) -> u64 {
    bytes.iter().filter(|&&b| b == b'\n').count() as u64
}
```

Hmm — wait, but there's a subtlety: when comment is enabled (after fix 1), `\n` is its own class so scan_and_copy never consumes `\n`. When comment is disabled and term is Any, `\n` is class 0 and gets copied — count needed. When term is CRLF, `\n` has a class → not copied. So counting in the range is correct in all cases.

### Fix 3: NFA line counting

Add to `read_record_nfa` and `read_field_nfa` loops. In both, the consume points are CopyToOutput and Discard. Add:

```rust
NfaInputAction::CopyToOutput => {
    output[nout] = input[nin];
    self.line += (input[nin] == b'\n') as u64;
    nout += 1;
    nin += 1;
}
NfaInputAction::Discard => {
    self.line += (input[nin] == b'\n') as u64;
    nin += 1;
}
```

Wait, but careful about CRLF: with CRLF terminator, `\r\n` — `\r` consumed (no count), `\n` consumed (+1). ✓ "CRLF 中只按 LF 加一次，单独的 CR 不增加行号". ✓

But hmm — does the DFA count match NFA count in all cases? DFA counts every consumed byte once (main loop + scan_and_copy fix). NFA counts every consumed byte once. ✓

Now — is there an issue with the DFA counting when a byte is consumed but the loop breaks? In read_record_dfa, line increment happens before `nin += 1`... let me re-check:

```rust
while nin < input.len() && nout < output.len() && nend < ends.len() {
    let (s, has_out) = self.dfa.get_output(state, input[nin]);
    self.line += (input[nin] == b'\n') as u64;
    state = s;
    ...
    nin += 1;
```

The byte at nin is always consumed (nin += 1) after counting. ✓. In read_field_dfa same pattern. ✓

Now, "没有消耗输入的调用不能改变行号" — empty-input calls go through transition_final paths, no counting. ✓

### Now check: does anything else depend on chunk boundaries for line numbers?

The `read_record` wrapper (BOM handling) — replay path: BOM bytes contain no `\n`. ✓

### Higher-level: Serde positions, byte/string record positions

These flow from core.line() → fixed.

### csv-index RandomAccessSimple

"用同样配置创建 RandomAccessSimple 索引时，注释不得成为索引项" — csv-index simple.rs is identical to upstream; it uses ReaderBuilder from the csv crate... let me check csv-index/src/simple.rs to see how it creates the reader and whether comments would become index entries. Since the DFA comment bug caused comments to swallow data and produce phantom records, fixing csv-core fixes the index too. But wait — csv-index's RandomAccessSimple::create uses `ReaderBuilder::new()...from_reader` — does it expose comment/terminator config? Let me look.

